                "text": "**Analyzing Color Block Segments**\n\nI'm now focusing on the lengths of the contiguous color segments and zero segments in the input. I'm seeing patterns emerge based on these segment sizes. This new approach might provide a more direct path to understanding the problem's core mechanics.\n\n\n**Observing Zero Separation**\n\nI've been meticulously examining the zero segments and how they relate to the colored blocks. It appears the zeros consistently maintain their role as separators between the blocks in both the input and output. Furthermore, their positions seem to correspond to block separations. I'm focusing now on the number of zero rows between blocks and observing the impact of sorting the blocks.\n\n\n",
